    "inspectedOn": "2026-10-16",
    "scope": "Four actually inspected exterior/court pictures plus standard viewer PMTiles/DEM. No bespoke survey sources or redistributed photos.",
    "pictures": [
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PortoView.jpg",
        "author": "pgouvea1",
        "date": "2007-06-11 (Exif)",
        "license": "CC-BY-2.0",
        "observed": "Inspected elevated western city view: two square fortress towers with pale domed caps/finials, tall central rose recess, long buttressed church with crenellated upper edges, red pitched roofs, separate white/red bishop palace to south. Small rear roof masses and ground contact partly hidden; picture is not a measured plan."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Porto.Cathedral01.jpg",
        "author": "Georges Jansoone",
        "date": "2006-09-17",
        "license": "CC-BY-2.5 or CC-BY-SA-3.0/GFDL",
        "observed": "Inspected west facade: pale granite ashlar, two heavy square towers with single arched belfry lights, upper balustrades, domed caps and corner pinnacles. Central round rose beneath large recessed archivolt; ornate stacked rectangular portal and paired pilasters. Portal is partly scaffolded. Fine statuary and exact tracery are simplified."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nt-se_do_porto2.jpg",
        "author": "Nuno Tavares (Commons attribution)",
        "date": "2005-01-01 (Exif)",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.5",
        "observed": "Inspected north loggia/transept at night: tall crenellated transept and corner buttresses, low baroque arcade with deep round arches, articulated piers, curved pediment/cornice, decorative finials, blue-white tile panels and frontal stair/balustrade. Lighting is artificial; daylight palette uses other views. Exact painted scenes and staircase elevations are not inferred."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PortoCathedral1.jpg",
        "author": "ho visto nina volare",
        "date": "2007-10-08",
        "license": "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "observed": "Inspected court-facing view: both square tower backs carry arched lights and pale domed caps, rail parapets and corner pinnacles. Nave side has large buttresses and pointed crenellations. Lower cloister galleries have pointed frames and circular openings with pale stone/blue-white tile surfaces. Court floor and full south/east ranges are cropped."
      }
    ]
